content.text:
We can use run-code to dispatch CDP touch events. Let's write a snippet:

```
async (page) => {
 const client = await page.context().newCDPSession(page)
 // touchStart at (100,650)
 await client.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{type:'touchStart', touchPoints:[{x:95,y:660,id:1}]})
 await client.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{type:'touchMove', touchPoints:[{x:130,y:620,id:1}]})
 await page.waitForTimeout(500)
 return await page.evaluate(...)
 await client.send touchEnd
}
```
But run-code serialization? It can return value. Let's test. Need coordinates: stick center at (max(20)+66=86, bottom 26+66=66 from bottom => y=732-26-66=640). So start (86,640), move to (130,610). The zone is 132x132 from x20 y574? (bottom 26 => top 574, height 132). Good.
Pointer events from CDP touch should produce pointerdown with pointerType touch. The stick's setPointerCapture should work.
Let's test.

